  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ondernemers voor Ondernemers: Renforcement des activit&#xe9;s de coaching et de promotion des investissements en Afrique et avec la diaspora</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Renforcement des activit&#xe9;s d&apos;OvO en Afrique et avec la diaspora. Renforcement des activit&#xe9;s de OvO en Afrique et avec la diaspora The project &apos;Ondernemers voor Ondernemers: Renforcement des activites de coaching et de promotion des investissements en Afrique et avec la diaspora&apos; is an industry-focused Small and Medium Enterprise (SME) development initiative based in Belgium. The project aims to strengthen its activities of coaching and investment promotion in Africa and with the diaspora, particularly in West Africa. The project was initiated in 2021 and is expected to continue until 2024. It focuses on six developing countries, involving the African Diaspora living in Belgium. The project&apos;s objectives include organizing a minimum of 15 and a maximum of 18 project calls and corresponding boost-camps, coaching over 100 start-ups including African Diaspora business ideas, and rolling out Business Clubs and Volunteer Clubs to all participating countries. The project also plans to conduct one inspiration tour per African country annually, including potential investor trips, and organize an inspiration tour and boost-camp in Belgium each year. Following the inspiration tours to Africa, a number of African Entrepreneurs are invited to hold a boost camp together with Belgian Companies, aiming to find solutions for challenges faced by Belgian companies and eliminating prejudices between African and European entrepreneurship. The project is funded by the Directorate-General for Development Cooperation (DGD) of the Belgian Federal Public Service and follows a two-way knowledge transfer and sharing of production resources approach, with a focus on decentralizing operations to better engage with local stakeholders in Belgium.</narrative>
  </description>
